Z||000000||newfie||10-14-2001||01:55 PM||||I'm a Canadian and up here good shape fiero's are few and far between.  I'm going to be down in the Southern states working for a few months after XMAS.  Thinking about buying while down there. What kinda of things have to be considered.  I don't what the policies are on taxes, inspections, duties stuff like that down in the U.S. Anyone help me out on the details?||||reg||5
Z||000001||hutch84fierose||10-14-2001||03:38 PM||||i don't have the awnser at all to you question but I was wondering kinda the same information sort of.  I live in ontario canada and I was thinking of ording some stuff for the Fiero in the US.  Now the same thing what has to be considered before i go and do this.  And have it shipped here of course to what do i need to know again thanks for the help everyone||||reg||1
Z||000002||Master_Sushi||10-14-2001||07:53 PM||||I believe there is a 300-500$ fee to get a title transferred over from US-Canada, Either way. You can call the border and ask them. They have a special agency for this stuff at every border crossing. Give um’ a ring! They will have all the details. Everything I know if just from what I’ve heard other people say! So I might not be right.||||reg||1
Z||000003||72vinman||10-14-2001||07:58 PM||||Hi guys, prior to buying my GT I had look at all the info for this.<BR>Newfie, If you buy a car south of the border there a re a few things you need to do.<BR>1. You need a letter from a Pomtiac dealer stating that the car has had all recall work done. Just drop by the closest dealership and give them the VIN number. They will give you a printout for customs.<BR>2. When you get to the border you have to by an import fee which if I remember coreectly it was $140 CDN. You will also have to pay GST on the purchase price so have whoever you buy the car from just write up an invoice for $200<BR>3.Customs will take information about the car and your on your way home. In a few days the send you some forms to fill out and the car must pass a safety within 14 days I think. <BR>This is just off the top of my head. If you need more detailed info email me and I will try to find the info. It is in my office at work.<BR>Good Luck<P>||||reg||1
